              <p style=3D"margin:0 0 18px 0;font-size:14px;color:#444444;li=
ne-height:1.8;">The rapid advancement of large language models =E2=80=94 in=
cluding systems like Claude, GPT-4, and Gemini =E2=80=94 has introduced a n=
ew class of threat to cryptocurrency security. Attackers are leveraging AI =
to generate highly convincing phishing campaigns, automate social engineeri=
ng at scale, write exploit code faster than ever, and probe wallet interfac=
es for behavioral vulnerabilities that traditional tools would miss entirel=
y.</p>

              <p style=3D"margin:0 0 18px 0;font-size:14px;color:#444444;li=
ne-height:1.8;">These are not opportunistic attacks. AI-assisted hacks are =
increasingly targeted, adaptive, and difficult to distinguish from legitima=
te interactions. The volume and sophistication of incidents tied to AI tool=
ing has grown sharply over the past twelve months, and the barrier to execu=
ting them continues to fall.</p>

              <p style=3D"margin:0 0 32px 0;font-size:14px;color:#444444;li=
ne-height:1.8;">To address this, Ledger is rolling out AI-Resistant Firmwar=
e as part of Ledger OS 2.1. This update introduces behavioral anomaly detec=
tion directly on the Secure Element, hardens the device against AI-generate=
d transaction manipulation, and adds a new confirmation layer that flags re=
quests matching known AI-assisted attack patterns. Your seed phrase never l=
eaves the device. No action is required beyond installing the update.</p>

